Test-only dependencies
----------------------
The test projects reference Jellyfin 12.2.0 (GPL-3.0-only),
Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.14.1 (MIT; Microsoft Corporation), and xUnit 2.9.3 /
xunit.runner.visualstudio 3.1.5 (Apache-2.0; James Newkirk, Brad Wilson and the
.NET Foundation). Their installed NuGet metadata supplies these declarations.
Optional coverage uses Coverlet and the versions locked in
tools/coverage/package-lock.json: v8-to-istanbul 9.3.0 (ISC),
istanbul-lib-coverage 3.2.2, istanbul-lib-report 3.0.1 and istanbul-reports 3.2.0
(BSD-3-Clause). Each tool keeps its own license in its separate installation. Those
tools, runtime distributions and their dependencies are downloaded separately,
not redistributed in the plugin ZIP (Jellyfin.Plugin.Babelfin.dll, LICENSE,
NOTICE, logo.png and meta.json) or corresponding-source archive.
The native-policy checker invokes Jellyfin's own policy from an installed
server assembly for comparison. It does not redistribute that assembly or copy
its implementation.

Other shipped material and corresponding source
----------------------------------------------
The Babelfin HTML/CSS/JavaScript, inline icons, logo and translations
are included in this project. No third-party fonts,
browser frameworks, competitor-plugin code or competitor translations are
bundled. Jellyfin DOM/API compatibility and observed behavior are not presented
as ownership of Jellyfin code.

AI tools are used for development, review and all translations. Tested with Jellyfin 12.4 and the Jellyfin Android app on Google Pixel 11 Pro XL. Automated integration tests use Jellyfin Web on a disposable Jellyfin 12.2 test instance. Android TV, Swiftfin, Streamyfin and physical TVs have not been tested.

The corresponding-source archive contains the complete tracked source tree,
embedded assets, the pinned language input and generator, and build/install
scripts. It contains no Git history, downloaded runtimes or private artifacts.
See README and CONTRIBUTING for building and testing; SOURCE.json in the source
archive identifies its exact commit, tree, intended release tag and version.
